From: Frederik van Hövell
Subject: [PATCH] hw/misc/bcm2835_property: return the framebuffer GPU bus alias

Adapted to the pinned QEMU 10.2.4 headers from the author's QEMU-devel
submission dated 2026-08-19:
https://www.mail-archive.com/qemu-devel@nongnu.org/msg1217399.html

The allocation property returns a VideoCore bus address. EDK2 subtracts
0xc0000000 and Linux masks its upper alias bits to recover a CPU address.
QEMU already maps this GPU bus alias; retain the internal framebuffer base
and fix only the mailbox wire response.

--- a/hw/misc/bcm2835_property.c
+++ b/hw/misc/bcm2835_property.c
@@ -227,7 +227,8 @@
         /* Frame buffer */
 
         case RPI_FWREQ_FRAMEBUFFER_ALLOCATE:
-            stl_le_phys(&s->dma_as, value + 12, fbconfig.base);
+            stl_le_phys(&s->dma_as, value + 12,
+                        fbconfig.base | BCM2836_DMA_DEVICE_OFFSET);
             stl_le_phys(&s->dma_as, value + 16,
                         bcm2835_fb_get_size(&fbconfig));
             resplen = 8;
--- a/include/hw/display/bcm2835_fb.h
+++ b/include/hw/display/bcm2835_fb.h
@@ -15,7 +15,8 @@
 #include "hw/sysbus.h"
 #include "qom/object.h"
 
-#define UPPER_RAM_BASE 0x40000000
+#define UPPER_RAM_BASE            0x40000000
+#define BCM2836_DMA_DEVICE_OFFSET 0xc0000000
 
 #define TYPE_BCM2835_FB "bcm2835-fb"
 OBJECT_DECLARE_SIMPLE_TYPE(BCM2835FBState, BCM2835_FB)
